         ("Inflammation is trapping stored iron so little reaches the marrow", True, "Inflammation raises hepcidin, which locks iron inside storage cells. Ferritin rises with stores and inflammation, while the low TSAT shows little iron is available for red-cell production."),
         ("He has iron overload, which is the direct cause of his anemia", False, "A high ferritin with a low TSAT does not indicate overload causing anemia; ferritin also rises with inflammation."),
